1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:18,146
I drove off the broken bridge because the bridge had stopped being
useful. Nigga, I gave that bridge several chances. The Lamborghini
left the stone ledge and landed on a maintenance platform hanging
below it. The suspension slammed hard enough to make my teeth click.

2
00:00:18,396 --> 00:00:40,093
Shawna caught the handle over her door and shouted something that
began with my name and ended with a detailed opinion of my judgment. I
agreed with the passionate parts. Ahead, a blue service lane flickered
between the platform and the stadium's outer ring. It was narrower
than a proper road and less confident about existing.

3
00:00:40,343 --> 00:01:06,924
The Heart's unstable field kept making pieces of it fade. I watched
the light pulse. Waited one breath. Then drove. The wheels caught the
lane at its brightest point. We raced through open air while the path
went dim behind us. Below, clouds climbed toward the academy's falling
edges. Above, Voss's aircraft crossed toward the central tower. Shawna
stared through the windshield. Aiden.

4
00:01:07,174 --> 00:01:30,586
I see it. You see all of it? Nigga, I'm trying to focus on the helpful
portion. The lane ended short of the stadium ring. I didn't brake. The
Lamborghini flew the gap and struck the ring road with its front
wheels first. The rear swung wide. I corrected, straightened, and
heard a roar from the field below. People had seen us. People were
cheering.

5
00:01:30,836 --> 00:01:54,546
Nigga, I needed those people to evacuate, but I understood the
interruption. Knox looked up from beside a helicopter and put both
hands on her head. That's my fucking captain, she said over the radio.
Pike answered from the control entrance. He's technically ours this
week. Commander, don't get greedy. I took the last turn toward the
central chamber.

6
00:01:54,796 --> 00:02:18,690
Voss's aircraft had landed through its glass roof. Not on it. Through
it. Broken panels lay across the terrace. Smoke rose from the
aircraft's nose. He had abandoned any interest in returning school
property in good condition. Shawna and I got out. Inside, Storm stood
between Voss and the Heart. Her hands were white with restrained
lightning.

7
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:42,739
She looked exhausted enough to fall but remained exactly where she had
chosen to stand. Behind her, Bell's assistants sheltered near the
wall. Lena crouched beside one whose leg was trapped under a fallen
beam. She was speaking in a calm voice that belonged entirely to her
now. Voss raised his staff. You cannot hold it forever. Storm's eyes
burned.

8
00:02:42,989 --> 00:03:06,157
You keep mistaking exhaustion for agreement. He struck. White light
met blue. The room shook. I ran toward the trapped assistant while
Shawna moved around the opposite side. Together we lifted the beam
enough for Lena to pull him clear. The assistant looked at me,
recognized me, and began thanking me while he was still being dragged
across the floor.

9
00:03:06,407 --> 00:03:30,432
Nigga, thank me in the hallway. Move. He moved. Voss saw me. His face
did something beautiful and ugly at once: astonishment because I had
arrived again, hatred because apparently arriving was a talent he
could not buy. What are you? I stepped into the open. Consistent. He
turned the staff toward me. Shawna fired. The staff broke near its
head.

10
00:03:30,682 --> 00:03:55,298
Blue force burst sideways into the Heart's housing. Glass cracked. The
core's light flared so bright every shadow in the room vanished. Storm
threw both hands toward it. The surge struck her and drove her to her
knees. Bell's voice came through the radio. The transfer conductor is
open. Get away from the housing. Voss's armor began drinking the loose
current.

11
00:03:55,548 --> 00:04:10,727
He smiled through the pain. The nigga was still trying to win with a
mouthful of the disaster he had made. Then the ceiling support above
Shawna began to fall. I saw it. Saw her look up. Saw the distance
between us.

12
00:04:10,977 --> 00:04:27,003
There was no time for a clever route, no car, no faculty member with a
gift ready to do the part my body could not reach. I ran. The broken
transfer conductor lay across the floor between us, black metal
wrapped in blue light.

13
00:04:27,253 --> 00:04:48,933
It was part of Voss's attempt to bond a human body to the Heart's
charge, a system he had forced Bell's designs into and Reiss had
warned him not to use. I stepped over it. It caught my leg. Current
tore through me. Nigga, I had never known pain could be a color. Blue
filled my hands. My chest. My mouth.

14
00:04:49,183 --> 00:05:11,220
Every muscle locked, then opened into a terrible fast clarity. The
falling beam seemed to move slowly enough for me to see the chips of
paint leaving its edge. It wasn't slow. I was moving. I reached
Shawna. Caught her around the waist. We crossed the room in a flash
that left blue fire crawling along the floor behind us.

15
00:05:11,470 --> 00:05:33,978
The beam struck where she had stood. I hit the wall with her in my
arms and fell to one knee. The light went out. For a moment I could
not breathe. Shawna held my face. Aiden. I tried to answer. Nothing
came. My hands shook violently. Tiny blue threads moved beneath the
skin, then faded. The old wound still hurt.

16
00:05:34,228 --> 00:05:58,036
My bruised ribs still hurt. Whatever had happened had not repaired a
single fucking thing. It had simply made me do something impossible
and sent the bill directly to my body. Storm stared at me from beside
the broken housing. Voss stared too. Bell arrived at the doorway with
Miriam behind him and stopped so abruptly she nearly walked into his
back.

17
00:05:58,286 --> 00:06:22,816
You bonded with the conductor, he said. I finally found enough air for
words. Nigga, was there a cheaper option? Shawna laughed once, half
relief and half terror. Then she pulled me against her so tightly my
ribs filed another complaint. Voss raised his armored hand. That power
is mine. Tank came through the doorway behind Bell. He looked at my
glowing fingers.

18
00:06:23,066 --> 00:06:46,533
Looked at Voss. Nigga, ain't nothing about this man ever belonged to
you. He fired. Voss ducked behind the Heart's damaged housing. Storm
used the moment to pull the loose current back into a contained arc.
Bell and Miriam reached the emergency braces. Shawna helped me stand.
My legs felt like somebody had replaced the bones with hot wire.

19
00:06:46,783 --> 00:07:11,572
Victor arrived through the roof opening and looked straight at me. He
could feel it. I saw that in his face before he spoke. You didn't have
that before. Nigga, I had several other advantages. He smiled despite
everything. Of course you did. Voss tore a black coupling from the
housing and leaped back toward his aircraft. The core itself remained
inside the emergency braces.

20
00:07:11,822 --> 00:07:37,187
He had taken a concentrated store of charge, enough to keep his armor
alive while the Heart continued supporting the school. The aircraft's
engines whined. Tank fired at its rising nose. Victor forced it away
from the open roof with a burst of lightning. Voss escaped through the
gap anyway, his damaged craft dragging sparks into the morning air.
The stadium shuddered again.

21
00:07:37,437 --> 00:08:03,628
Bell shouted from the braces. We have to reset the outer support ring.
Now. The western section is breaking loose. I looked toward the
windows. A quarter of the stadium's outer structure had begun sliding
away from the island. People crowded the stairs leading off it. A
helicopter hovered too far away to reach everyone before the stone
separated. My Lamborghini waited on the terrace.

22
00:08:03,878 --> 00:08:24,872
Blue threads flickered in my fingers. Shawna saw both things at once.
Can you control it? Don't know yet. Then listen to me. One thing. One
burst. You don't spend yourself like you're infinite. I looked at her.
The word infinite had never sounded more like a trap than it did in
her mouth. I nodded. One thing.

23
00:08:25,122 --> 00:08:45,860
Bell showed us the outer support arch from the window. Its emergency
return point sat along the stadium road, just beyond the widening gap.
A powered vehicle could carry a short charge across it and wake the
local field long enough for the engineers to secure it. Yesterday that
would have meant Victor's car.

24
00:08:46,110 --> 00:09:09,354
Victor's car had burned because Voss wanted to turn a man into fuel.
Today my hands glowed. I wasn't going to let Voss decide what that
meant too. I got into the Lamborghini. Shawna got in beside me before
I could start an argument we had already settled a hundred ways. Tank
leaned through my window. Nigga, you got lightning now? Little bit.

25
00:09:09,604 --> 00:09:32,479
That nigga was already too much. They gave that nigga electricity.
Victor stood behind him, smiling with exhausted wonder. Blue Thunder,
Shawna said. We all looked at her. She touched my hand on the wheel.
That's what it looked like. I smiled. Baby, you naming my greatness?
Somebody has to keep it organized. I started the engine.

26
00:09:32,729 --> 00:09:55,066
The new charge moved when I wanted it to. Not easily. Not painlessly.
I felt it gather in my arms, felt my heartbeat grow hard and quick,
felt the Lamborghini answer with a low blue shimmer across its dark
paint. Then we moved. The car shot along the stadium ring faster than
it had ever moved under its own engine.

27
00:09:55,316 --> 00:10:19,214
The world sharpened around the windshield. Every broken edge, every
loose stone, every opening in the road seemed to arrive with just
enough time for my hands to answer. The gap opened ahead. I held the
wheel. Blue light crossed the hood. We jumped. For one brief burst the
car carried my charge through the empty space between the two pieces
of road.

28
00:10:19,464 --> 00:10:44,580
The local field caught it, flared, and held. The Lamborghini landed
beneath the support arch in a thunderclap that rolled across the
stadium. The sliding section stopped. People on the stairs caught one
another instead of falling. The engineers' lights turned green. My
hands went dark. So did the edges of my vision. Shawna caught the
wheel while I fought to keep my head up.

29
00:10:44,830 --> 00:11:06,239
She guided us into the safe bay beside the arch and brought the car to
a stop. I leaned forward, breathing hard enough to hurt. One burst,
she said, holding the back of my neck. I nodded. Could not speak yet.
Below us, the stadium began cheering. Above us, Voss's aircraft
circled back toward the tower.

30
00:11:06,489 --> 00:11:15,988
Inside my car, my wife kept her hand on my neck until my breathing
slowed. Blue Thunder had arrived. Nigga, I still needed a minute.
